Q: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property &#39;submit&#39; of null A: <pre><code>

If document.getElementById(&quot;form1&quot;) returns null, it means the browser can't find the form when verificar() runs.

Two common reasons:
1. Your script runs before the form is loaded in the DOM.
2. You have duplicate id=&quot;form1&quot; somewhere else on the page (check included PHP files).

Try this safer version:

function verificar(){
    if(certoCarga &amp;&amp; certoKm){
        var form = document.getElementById(&quot;form1&quot;);
        if(form){
            form.submit();
        } else {
            console.log(&quot;form not found - check duplicate IDs&quot;);
        }
    }
}

To debug, open browser console and type:
document.querySelectorAll(&quot;#form1&quot;)
If it returns more than one element, you have a duplicate ID problem.
</code></pre>

Q: How can I pass an immediate array to a C function accepting pointer? A: <p>You can simply make the array parameter to be of reference type, that is, pass the array by reference. Then to accept any array use NTTP as shown below:</p>
<pre><code>template&lt;std::size_t N&gt;
int func_1(int param_1, const int (&amp;arr_1)[N]){return {};}

int main()
{
        int var_1 = 1;
    int var_2 = 2;
    int var_3 = 3;

    int var_4 = func_1(var_1, {var_2, var_3}); //works 
    int var_5 = func_1(var_1, {2,3,var_3}); //also works 
}
</code></pre>
